 for Remote Execution\",\"name\":\"Debugging Remote Cache Hits for Remote Execution\",\"url\":\"https://bazel.build/remote/cache-remote\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@id\":\"https://bazel.build/remote/cache-remote#webpage\"},\"dateModified\":\"2026-08-06T10:58:30.536Z\",\"publisher\":{\"@id\":\"https://bazel.build/#organization\"},\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https://bazel.build#website\"}}]}"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"38:T3859,"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"\"use strict\";const{Fragment:_Fragment,jsx:_jsx,jsxs:_jsxs}=arguments[0];const{useMDXComponents:_provideComponents}=arguments[0];function _createMdxContent(props){const _components={a:`a`,br:`br`,code:`code`,li:`li`,ol:`ol`,p:`p`,pre:`pre`,span:`span`,..._provideComponents(),...props.components},{CodeBlock,Heading}=_components;if(!CodeBlock)_missingMdxReference(`CodeBlock`,true);if(!Heading)_missingMdxReference(`Heading`,true);return _jsxs(_Fragment,{children:[_jsx(_components.p,{children:`This page describes how to check your cache hit rate and how to investigate\ncache misses in the context of remote execution.`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`This page assumes that you have a build and/or test that successfully\nutilizes remote execution, and you want to ensure that you are effectively\nutilizing remote cache.`}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`check-cache-hits`,children:`Checking your cache hit rate`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`In the standard output of your Bazel run, look at the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`INFO`}),` line that lists\nprocesses, which roughly correspond to Bazel actions. That line details\nwhere the action was run. Look for the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`remote`}),` label, which indicates an action\nexecuted remotely, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`linux-sandbox`}),` for actions executed in a local sandbox,\nand other values for other execution strategies. An action whose result came\nfrom a remote cache is displayed as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`remote cache hit`}),`.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`For example:`}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`2`,language:`text`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`text`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`text`,numberOfLines:`2`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{children:`INFO: 11 processes: 6 remote cache hit, 3 internal, 2 remote.`})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{})})]})})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`In this example there were 6 remote cache hits, and 2 actions did not have\ncache hits and were executed remotely. The 3 internal part can be ignored.\nIt is typically tiny internal actions, such as creating symbolic links. Local\ncache hits are not included in this summary. If you are getting 0 processes\n(or a number lower than expected), run `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`bazel clean`}),` followed by your build/test\ncommand.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`troubleshooting-cache-hits`,children:`Troubleshooting cache hits`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`If you are not getting the cache hit rate you are expecting, do the following:`}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`rerun-cache-hits`,children:`Ensure re-running the same build/test command produces cache hits`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ol,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Run the build(s) and/or test(s) that you expect to populate the cache. The\nfirst time a new build is run on a particular stack, you can expect no remote\ncache hits. As part of remote execution, action results are stored in the\ncache and a subsequent run should pick them up.`}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Run `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`bazel clean`}),`. This command cleans your local cache, which allows\nyou to investigate remote cache hits without the results being masked by\nlocal cache hits.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Run the build(s) and test(s) that you are investigating again (on the same\nmachine).`}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Check the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`INFO`}),` line for cache hit rate. If you see no processes except\n`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`remote cache hit`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`internal`}),`, then your cache is being correctly populated and\naccessed. In that case, skip to the next section.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`A likely source of discrepancy is something non-hermetic in the build causing\nthe actions to receive different action keys across the two runs. To find\nthose actions, do the following:`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`a. Re-run the build(s) or test(s) in question to obtain execution logs:`}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`4`,language:`text`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`text`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`text`,numberOfLines:`4`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{children:`bazel clean`})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{children:`bazel \u003cvar\u003e--optional-flags\u003c/var\u003e build //\u003cvar\u003eyour:target\u003c/var\u003e --execution_log_compact_file=/tmp/exec1.log`})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{})})]})})}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`b. `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#compare-logs`,children:`Compare the execution logs`}),` between the\ntwo runs. Ensure that the actions are identical across the two log files.\nDiscrepancies provide a clue about the changes that occurred between the\nruns. Update your build to eliminate those discrepancies.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`If you are able to resolve the caching problems and now the repeated run\nproduces all cache hits, skip to the next section.`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`If your action IDs are identical but there are no cache hits, then something\nin your configuration is preventing caching. Continue with this section to\ncheck for common problems.`}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Check that all actions in the execution log have `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`cacheable`}),` set to true. If\n`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`cacheable`}),` does not appear in the execution log for a give action, that\nmeans that the corresponding rule may have a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`no-cache`}),` tag in its\ndefinition in the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`BUILD`}),` file. Look at the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`mnemonic`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`target_label`}),`\nfields in the execution log to help determine where the action is coming\nfrom.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`If the actions are identical and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`cacheable`}),` but there are no cache hits, it\nis possible that your command line includes `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--noremote_accept_cached`}),` which\nwould disable cache lookups for a build.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`If figuring out the actual command line is difficult, use the canonical\ncommand line from the\n`,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/remote/bep`,children:`Build Event Protocol`}),`\nas follows:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`a. Add `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--build_event_text_file=/tmp/bep.txt`}),` to your Bazel command to get\nthe text version of the log.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`b. Open the text version of the log and search for the\n`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`structured_command_line`}),` message with `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`command_line_label: \"canonical\"`}),`.\nIt will list all the options after expansion.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`c. Search for `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`remote_accept_cached`}),` and check whether it’s set to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`false`}),`.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`d. If `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`remote_accept_cached`}),` is `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`false`}),`, determine where it is being\nset to `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`false`}),`: either at the command line or in a\n`,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/run/bazelrc#bazelrc-file-locations`,children:`bazelrc`}),` file.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`caching-across-machines`,children:`Ensure caching across machines`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`After cache hits are happening as expected on the same machine, run the\nsame build(s)/test(s) on a different machine. If you suspect that caching is\nnot happening across machines, do the following:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ol,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Make a small modification to your build to avoid hitting existing caches.`}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Run the build on the first machine:`}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`4`,language:`text`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`text`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`text`,numberOfLines:`4`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{children:` bazel clean`})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{children:` bazel ... build ... --execution_log_compact_file=/tmp/exec1.log`})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{})})]})})}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Run the build on the second machine, ensuring the modification from step 1\nis included:`}),`\n`,_jsx(CodeBlock,{filename:``,numberOfLines:`4`,language:`text`,children:_jsx(_components.pre,{className:`shiki shiki-themes github-light-default dark-plus`,style:{backgroundColor:`#ffffff`,\"--shiki-dark-bg\":`#0B0C0E`,color:`#1f2328`,\"--shiki-dark\":`#D4D4D4`},language:`text`,children:_jsxs(_components.code,{language:`text`,numberOfLines:`4`,children:[_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{children:` bazel clean`})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{children:` bazel ... build ... --execution_log_compact_file=/tmp/exec2.log`})}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.span,{className:`line`,children:_jsx(_components.span,{})})]})})}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#compare-logs-the-execution-logs`,children:`Compare the execution logs`}),` for the two\nruns. If the logs are not identical, investigate your build configurations\nfor discrepancies as well as properties from the host environment leaking\ninto either of the builds.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`compare-logs`,children:`Comparing the execution logs`}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`The execution log contains records of actions executed during the build.\nEach record describes both the inputs (not only files, but also command line\narguments, environment variables, etc) and the outputs of the action. Thus,\nexamination of the log can reveal why an action was reexecuted.`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`The execution log can be produced in one of three formats:\ncompact (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--execution_log_compact_file`}),`),\nbinary (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--execution_log_binary_file`}),`) or JSON (`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`--execution_log_json_file`}),`).\nThe compact format is recommended, as it produces much smaller files with very\nlittle runtime overhead. The following instructions work for any format. You\ncan also convert between them using the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`//src/tools/execlog:converter`}),` tool.`]}),`\n`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`To compare logs for two builds that are not sharing cache hits as expected,\ndo the following:`}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.ol,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Get the execution logs from each build and store them as `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/tmp/exec1.log`}),` and\n`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/tmp/exec2.log`}),`.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Download the Bazel source code and build the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`//src/tools/execlog:parser`}),`\ntool:`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`git clone `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git`,children:`https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel.git`}),`\ncd bazel\nbazel build //src/tools/execlog:parser`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Use the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`//src/tools/execlog:parser`}),` tool to convert the logs into a\nhuman-readable text format. In this format, the actions in the second log are\nsorted to match the order in the first log, making a comparison easier.`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`bazel-bin/src/tools/execlog/parser `,_jsx(_components.br,{}),`\n`,`—log_path=/tmp/exec1.log `,_jsx(_components.br,{}),`\n`,`—log_path=/tmp/exec2.log `,_jsx(_components.br,{}),`\n`,`—output_path=/tmp/exec1.log.txt `,_jsx(_components.br,{}),`\n`,`—output_path=/tmp/exec2.log.txt`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`\n`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Use your favourite text differ to diff `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/tmp/exec1.log.txt`}),` and\n`,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/tmp/exec2.log.txt`}),`.`]}),`\n`]}),`\n`]})]})}function MDXContent(props={}){const{wrapper:MDXLayout}={..._provideComponents(),...props.components};return MDXLayout?_jsx(MDXLayout,{...props,children:_jsx(_createMdxContent,{...props})}):_createMdxContent(props)}return{default:MDXContent};function _missingMdxReference(id,component){throw new Error(`Expected `+(component?`component`:`object`)+\" `\"+id+\"` to be defined: you likely forgot to import, pass, or provide it.\")}"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"2c:[\"$\",\"$L2d\",null,{\"theme\":\"mint\",\"pageMetadata\":{\"title\":\"Debugging Remote Cache Hits for Remote Execution\",\"description\":null,\"href\":\"/remote/cache-remote\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2e\",null,{\"value\":{\"apiReferenceData\":{},\"graphqlReferenceData\":\"$undefined\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L2f\",null,{\"value\":{\"pageMetadata\":\"$2c:props:pageMetadata\",\"lastModified\":\"2026-08-06T10:58:30.536Z\",\"gitLastModified\":\"$undefined\",\"originalFileLocation\":\"remote/cache-remote.mdx\",\"description\":null,\"mdxExtracts\":{\"tableOfContents\":[{\"title\":\"Checking your cache hit rate\",\"slug\":\"check-cache-hits\",\"depth\":2,\"children\":[]},{\"title\":\"Troubleshooting cache hits\",\"slug\":\"troubleshooting-cache-hits\",\"depth\":2,\"children\":[{\"title\":\"Ensure re-running the same build/test command produces cache hits\",\"slug\":\"rerun-cache-hits\",\"depth\":3,\"children\":[]},{\"title\":\"Ensure caching across machines\",\"slug\":\"caching-across-machines\",\"depth\":3,\"children\":[]}]},{\"title\":\"Comparing the execution logs\",\"slug\":\"compare-logs\",\"depth\":2,\"children\":[]}],\"codeExamples\":{}},\"pageType\":\"$undefined\",\"panelMdxSource\":\"$undefined\",\"panelMdxSourceWithNoJs\":\"$undefined\",\"contextualStarterQuestions\":\"$undefined\",\"relatedPages\":\"$undefined\"},\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L30\",null,{\"pageMetadata\":\"$2c:props:pageMetadata\",\"mdxExtracts\":\"$2c:props:children:props:children:props:value:mdxExtracts\",\"openApiReferenceData\":\"$undefined\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L31\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$32\"}}],[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-page-mode', \\\"none\\\");\"}}],[\"$\",\"$L33\",null,{\"pageMetadata\":\"$2c:props:pageMetadata\"}]],[\"$\",\"$L34\",null,{\"pageMetadata\":\"$2c:props:pageMetadata\"}],[],[\"$\",\"$L35\",null,{\"customJsDisabled\":false,\"jsFiles\":[]}],[\"$\",\"$L36\",null,{\"slug\":\"remote/cache-remote\",\"pageMetadata\":\"$2c:props:pageMetadata\",\"theme\":\"mint\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L37\",null,{\"mdxSource\":{\"compiledSource\":\"$38\",\"frontmatter\":{},\"scope\":{\"config\":{},\"pageMetadata\":{\"title\":\"Debugging Remote Cache Hits for Remote Execution\",\"description\":null,\"href\":\"/remote/cache-remote\"}}},\"mdxSourceWithNoJs\":\"$undefined\",\"displayDomain\":\"bazel.build\"}]}]]}]}]}]}]}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"39:I[707934,[\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/19ae1768f166fab9.js?dpl=dpl_6FYZ3SECAF7eWA496xdtRigGS2Lx\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/b664fc8bb1e7ab0d.js?dpl=dpl_6FYZ3SECAF7eWA496xdtRigGS2Lx\",\"/mintlify-assets/_next/static/chunks/f5976305ab1768eb.js?dpl=dpl_6FYZ3S